architect › The job is done.

`SlidingWindow` is implemented in `src/window.ts` and tested in `src/window.test.ts`, committed on `work/main` as `e061e93`.

What changed:
- Constructor throws `RangeError` when `limit < 1` or `windowMs < 1`.
- `allow(key)` reads the clock once, prunes timestamps `<= now - windowMs` (so an event exactly `windowMs` old no longer counts), and records only if the pruned count is under the limit.
- `remaining(key)` prunes the same way and returns how many more events the key may have, without recording.

